Checked by reading the copy:
(a) fresh directory per job: solve() uses tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=f"s_{k}_", dir=WORK) for every
    CaDiCaL + cake_lpr job; march() uses tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=f"m_{tag}_", dir=WORK) for every
    split. Each directory is removed after its job. WORK=/opt/work/tmp.
(b) atomic writes: finalize().atomic() writes leaves.icnf and open.icnf to tempfile.mkstemp in the
    output dir, then os.replace() into place.
(c) first record: when leaves.jsonl does not exist, the first record written is
    {"case": a.name, "case_sha256": sha256(CASE.cnf)}; run with --name U_L6.
Also: a leaf is written to leaves.icnf only if status == "UNSAT" and cake_lpr == "s VERIFIED UNSAT"
(AUDIT BUG-1); cubes files are written via tmp + rename (RISK-1); this is the reviewed F2 driver,
unmodified (RISK-3). --skip is not used.
